<h1>About Country Compare</h1>

<div class="card">
  <p>Country Compare lets you compare two countries using real data from the World Bank.</p>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose two different countries.</li>
    <li>Choose an indicator: GDP per capita, population, life expectancy or internet users.</li>
    <li>Choose a range of years and click Compare.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Data source</h2>
  <p>
    World Bank Indicators API:
    <a href="https://datahelpdesk.worldbank.org/knowledgebase/articles/889392-about-the-indicators-api-documentation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">API documentation</a>.
    Some years have no data, so the app skips empty values.
  </p>

  <h2>Built with</h2>
  <p>Node.js, Express, Axios and EJS.</p>
</div>
